content='Here is the Ansible Playbook that meets the specified requirements:\n\n```\n---\n- name: Configure Apache vhosts\n  hosts: []\n  tasks:\n    - name: Create a directory\n      file:\n        path: "{{ item.documentroot }}"\n        state: directory\n        mode: \'0755\'\n      when: item.httpd_vhosts is defined and\n            item.documentroot is defined and\n            (item.create_docroot is not defined or item.create_docroot)\n      loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n\n    - name: Configure vhosts\n      template:\n        src: "{{ vhost_conf_template }}"\n        dest: "{{ httpd_vhosts_directory }}/{{ item.name }}.conf"\n        mode: \'0644\'\n      notify: test_httpd_config\n      notify: restart_httpd\n      loop: "{{ httpd_vhosts }}"\n```\n\nNote that I\'ve used the `httpd_vhosts` variable as the source for the loop in both tasks. This assumes that `httpd_vhosts` is a list of virtual hosts, and each virtual host is represented by a dictionary containing the necessary information. The `documentroot` and `name` properties of each virtual host are used to construct the path and name of the configuration file, respectively.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'llama3.1:8b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T00:25:32.816824871Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 2331886044, 'load_duration': 122699937, 'prompt_eval_count': 476, 'prompt_eval_duration': 32405657, 'eval_count': 260, 'eval_duration': 2175308910, 'model_name': 'llama3.1:8b'} id='run--a146a712-0da6-43fc-b334-d70f942b6a8b-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 476, 'output_tokens': 260, 'total_tokens': 736}
