Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: This task is used to import another task file called assert.yml. This file likely contains assertions to validate the state of the system or the values of variables.

Task 2: Manage automatic service management
Description Task 2: This is a block task that will manage automatic service management based on the package manager and the value of the variable apt_autostart_state. If apt_autostart_state is "disabled", it will copy a script to /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d to prevent automatic service management. If apt_autostart_state is "enabled", it will remove the script to allow automatic service management. This task only runs when the package manager is apt.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
--- 

- name: Import assert.yml
  include: assert.yml

- name: Manage automatic service management
  block:
  - name: Manage automatic service management (apt)
    when: ansible_distribution == "Ubuntu"
    block:
      - name: Copy policy-rc.d script (disable auto-start)
        copy:
          content: "#!/bin/sh\nexit 101"
          dest: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d
          mode: '0755'
        when: apt_autostart_state == "disabled"
      - name: Remove policy-rc.d script (enable auto-start)
        file:
          path: /usr/sbin/policy-rc.d
          state: absent
        when: apt_autostart_state == "enabled"
  - name: Remove block (non-apt package manager)
    when: ansible_distribution != "Ubuntu"


