Ready\' in the Kubernetes API.\n\n4. Uncordon the node: If `rke2_drain_node_during_upgrade` is true, the playbook marks the node as schedulable again after it has been drained and upgraded.\n\n5. Wait for all pods to be ready again: If `rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_ready` is true, the playbook waits until all pods in the cluster are marked as \'Running\' or \'Succeeded\' in the Kubernetes API.\n\n6. Wait for all pods to pass readiness checks: If `rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_healthy` is true, the playbook waits until all pods in the cluster are ready to serve traffic.\n\nThe playbook uses the `kubectl` module to execute Kubernetes commands on the target node, and the `service` module to restart the RKE2 service. The `when` parameter is used to conditionally execute tasks based on the values of variables. The `retry` and `retries` parameters are used to implement retries for tasks that may fail. The `until` parameter is used to implement conditional logic for tasks.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'llama3.1:8b', 'created_at': '2025-10-16T00:47:22.508928807Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 6748493741, 'load_duration': 125667002, 'prompt_eval_count': 867, 'prompt_eval_duration': 140812004, 'eval_count': 770, 'eval_duration': 6480549559, 'model_name': 'llama3.1:8b'} id='run--caa874bf-8663-4326-a82d-0d8382ec88e0-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 867, 'output_tokens': 770, 'total_tokens': 1637}
